An applicant shall be granted a franchise or revocable license to provide telecommunications services, provided the city commission reasonably determines that the applicant has agreed to or meets the following factors and such terms, conditions and other factors as the city commission deems appropriate and not prohibited by applicable law:
(1) The adequacy of the proposed compensation to be paid to the city, including the value of any in-kind facilities and telecommunications services offered by the applicant to the city;
(2) The financial and technical ability of the applicant to construct and maintain a telecommunications system in the streets, and a certificate of public convenience or other authorization from the State or Federal Communications Commission permitting the applicant to provide telecommunications services in the city;
(3) The ability of the applicant to maintain the property of the city in good condition throughout the term of the franchise;
(4) The willingness and ability of the applicant to meet construction and physical requirements and to abide by all purpose and policy conditions, limitations and requirements with respect to the franchise, the public health, safety and welfare, and the city's management of streets; and
(5) Whether there is sufficient capacity in the city streets to accommodate the proposed cable and/or related equipment;
(6) The streets' capacity to accommodate additional utility, cable, and telecommunications facilities if the franchise or license is granted;
(7) The damage or disruption, if any to any public or private facilities, businesses, services, travel, or landscaping if the franchise or license is granted;
(8) The public interest in minimizing the cost, disruption of construction, the interruption of safe travel over the streets, or access to any and all underground utilities to the extent not prohibited by law, any other factors or considerations deemed pertinent by the city for safeguarding the interests of the city and the public.
In making any determination hereunder as to any application for a revocable license to provide private telecommunications services and in accordance with applicable law, the city commission may consider such factors as it deems appropriate and in the public interest, including, without limitation, the foregoing factors to the extent applicable.
(Ord. No. 16-2001, § 1, 9-17-01)

